      "text": "Yes! Alkaline earth metals have similar physical and chemical properties because they all belong to Group 2 of the periodic table and have 2 valence electrons.\n\nPhysical properties\n\nThey are generally silvery-gray, shiny metals.\n\nThey are good conductors of heat and electricity.\n\nThey are generally harder and denser than Group 1 metals.\n\nThey have relatively high melting points compared with Group 1 metals.\n\nChemical properties\n\nThey all have 2 valence electrons.\n\nThey tend to lose 2 electrons to form +2 ions.\n\nThey react with oxygen to form metal oxides.\n\nMany react with water to produce hydrogen gas and metal hydroxides.\n\nTheir reactivity generally increases down the group.\n\nWhy are their properties similar?\n\nBecause they all have 2 electrons in their outermost shell, they behave similarly during chemical reactions.\n\nImportant: Their properties are similar, but not identical. For example, calcium reacts with cold water much more readily than magnesium.\n\nRemember for a test: Alkaline earth metals have similar physical and chemical properties because they have the same number of valence electrons (2).",
      "visualHints": {
        "svg": 0,
